  "overview": "**Liquid** is a dark-first design system anchored on `rgb(0, 0, 0)` canvas surfaces with `#f7f7f8` primary ink (19.6:1 contrast) and `rgb(255, 179, 184)` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `Lato` (92px display down to 18px body), unified by `4px` base corner radius and subtle shadow elevation.\n\nMaintained by **Merck**. Source: published token package, package `@emdgroup-liquid/liquid`. Inventory: **91** colors, **41** typography steps, and **11** documented components (SEE LICENSE IN LICENSE.md license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 11 component tokens with documented paddings: `1.5rem`, `8px 12px`, `2px`, `6px 12px`, `10px 14px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `rgb(43, 43, 59)` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #f7f7f8 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Layered Shadow Model**: Uses documented shadows (`0 0.0625rem 0.25rem #0f1a2e26,0 0 0.0625rem #0f1a2e26`) paired with `color-mix(in srgb, #f7f7f8 14%, transparent)` borders for elevated overlays.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `rgb(255, 179, 184)` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `rgb(0, 0, 0)` (dark) with `#f7f7f8` primary text and `#f7f7f8` secondary labels.\n- Use `rgb(255, 179, 184)` with `#0b0b0c` text (11.6:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `Lato` headings with `Lato` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `4px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (4px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `rgb(43, 43, 59)` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #f7f7f8 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of dark polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `4px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input` fields and secondary buttons."
}
